From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 eMMC HS400 at 200 MHz

Raises the eMMC (mmc2) from 150 to 200 MHz. The SD node keeps 150 MHz and is
untouched.

This only makes sense together with `mmc-sunxi-a733-hs400-timing-selection`, and that is the whole point. Until now
every HS400 attempt on this board ran a *mixed* configuration:

  our timing (MODE_SEL/NEW_SAM_EN/SAM_PH set, CCLK_DIV=1) at 150 MHz
      -> reads mostly survive on retries, writes fail with cmd 25 WR DCE
  vendor timing (all four cleared) at 150 MHz          <- `mmc-sunxi-a733-hs400-timing-selection` alone
      -> reads collapse, partition table unreadable

Neither is a configuration anyone has ever shown to work. The vendor stack runs
the second timing at 200 MHz and writes this exact eMMC without a single error,
so the pair - vendor timing AND 200 MHz - is the one combination with evidence
behind it. Phase relationships scale with the clock; transplanting one half of a
proven pair onto the other half's frequency is what produced both failures above.

The 150 MHz cap itself came from `arm64-dts-allwinner-a733-add-sd-emmc` and was left in place by `arm64-dts-allwinner-a733-emmc-hs400` with the note
"200 MHz HS400 never locked on this board". That observation stands, but it was
made with our timing, which does not fit 200 MHz either - so it never tested this
combination. The note is not evidence against 200 MHz per se.

Two things this does not claim. It is not a fix for the write failure by itself;
`mmc-sunxi-a733-hs400-timing-selection` without this is disproved, and this without `mmc-sunxi-a733-hs400-timing-selection` is the state that already
failed to lock. And the clock path has to be watched: at 200 MHz the driver asks
for a 400 MHz module clock, and smhc2 carries CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT, so the
framework may retune a shared PLL output (pll-peri0-800m currently sits at
300 MHz for exactly that reason) rather than switching to pll-peri1-800m with a
divider the way the vendor does. Read SMHC2_CLK (0x02002D20) back on the board:
the vendor value is 0x83000001 (PERI1_800M, M=2 -> 400 MHz module / 200 MHz card).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -803,13 +803,13 @@
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc2_pins>, <&mmc2_clk_pins>,
 				    <&mmc2_ds_pins>;
 			vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
 			vqmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc1v8>;
 			bus-width = <8>;
-			max-frequency = <150000000>;
+			max-frequency = <200000000>;
 			non-removable;
 			cap-mmc-highspeed;
 			mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 			mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 			cap-mmc-hw-reset;
 			#address-cells = <1>;
